# GridQ — deployment environment variables (example). Copy to your host's secret/config store.
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy (this .example is gitignored from the image too). See docs/deployment.md.
#
# All are OPTIONAL: with none set, the app serves an open, ephemeral demo on 127.0.0.1:8000 locally
# (the container CMD binds 0.0.0.0:${PORT:-8000}).

# --- Networking -------------------------------------------------------------
# Managed hosts (Render/Railway/Cloud Run) inject PORT; the container CMD already honours it.
# PORT=8000

# --- Public-URL gate (recommended ON for a public deployment) ---------------
# Turns on HTTP Basic Auth in front of everything except /healthz and /static. Dormant if unset.
# Set this as a SECRET on the host (e.g. `fly secrets set ...`), never in a committed file.
# Only protects credentials when the host terminates TLS (Fly/Render/Railway/Cloud Run all do).
# GRIDQ_BASIC_AUTH=olly:change-me-to-a-strong-password

# --- Run store (user submissions) -------------------------------------------
# Where per-run records + uploaded half-hourly CSVs are written (gitignored; needs protection).
# Default in the image is /data/runs. Mount a volume at /data for durability; otherwise ephemeral.
# GRIDQ_RUN_STORE=/data/runs

# --- Assumptions library ----------------------------------------------------
# The image sets this to /app/assumptions. Override only if you relocate the assumption YAMLs.
# GRIDQ_ASSUMPTIONS_DIR=/app/assumptions

# --- Determinism pins (already set in the Dockerfile; here for non-Docker/buildpack hosts) ---
# Keep single-threaded numerics + UTC so the MILP stays byte-reproducible (D18/D22).
# TZ=UTC
# LANG=C.UTF-8
# LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
# OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
# OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
# MKL_NUM_THREADS=1
# NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1
# POLARS_MAX_THREADS=1

# --- Accounts: Google sign-in + per-user projects (2026-07-07) ---------------
# Optional. WITHOUT these, every browser still gets a private anonymous workspace (runs are
# scoped to the browser's signed session cookie); /auth/login explains the constraint honestly.
# To enable Google sign-in: create an OAuth "Web application" client in Google Cloud Console,
# add <public URL>/auth/callback as an authorised redirect URI, then set all three below.
# GRIDQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GRIDQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
# GRIDQ_OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE=https://your-public-host.example
# Session-cookie signing secret. PIN THIS in production: when unset a random per-boot secret is
# used and every session (sign-ins AND anonymous workspaces) resets on restart.
# GRIDQ_SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
